From 1aa23d98c606014f03908f4ea9f2ce8afaace946 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:34:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: a picture without its enhancement picture
 takes the RPU of its own access unit

An RPU travels in the access unit of its enhancement picture. Where the two
layers are coded in different picture order, the base picture of a packet
is another picture than the enhancement picture of that packet (in the FEL
test stream, 2822 of 2876), and the RPU that FFmpeg attaches to a base
picture is then the one of a neighbour. A paired picture takes the RPU of
its enhancement picture (dvbridge_fel_layer_metadata()), and a picture whose
access unit is not decoded the one of its mark (MEL). A base picture that
goes out without its enhancement picture kept the RPU carried with it: after
a seek or a resynchronization while the layer waits for a picture to start
at, the leading pictures of that picture, a picture that refers to one that
was not decoded, a late one. That is the metadata of another picture: its
mapping, its brightness, wrong at every cut.

The module now keeps the RPU of each enhancement access unit whose time it
knows, with the time of the base packet that brought it: an access unit that
is given to the decoder, and, in a stream that gives the times of its
enhancement pictures, one that it passes over while it waits for a picture
to start at. Where dvbridge_fel_take() answered 2 for a base picture of such
a time, it answers 4, with a frame that carries that RPU as coded and the
metadata the base decoder made of it (the ring that Kodi feeds,
dvbridge_fel_base_metadata()): the answer Kodi takes already for the
pictures of a MEL whose layer is not decoded. It answers 0 while that access
unit may still come in one of the next two base packets (by the times, an
access unit can come a packet after the base picture of its time), and while
the base picture that brought the RPU is still to come out of the base
decoder, which Kodi now says for each one (dvbridge_fel_base_picture());
never longer. Where it does not know the access unit (by picture order,
before the layer has started; an access unit without its time), the picture
keeps the RPU carried with it, as before.

Kodi sends some pictures out without their layer for reasons of its own
(late, the end of the base layer, the layer starting again): for those it
asks dvbridge_fel_layer_rpu(), which gives the same frame and never waits,
and only for a picture that could be paired, whose time is its own. The log
at the end says how many pictures without their enhancement picture had the
metadata of their own access unit.

Nothing changes for a paired picture: the frame of an answer 4 changes only
the metadata of a picture that goes out without the layer, through the rule
it has today. Tested on the host with the FEL test stream in one track and
in two (fel_rpu_test and fel_tracks_test, extended with what the stream says
of the time of each access unit): the whole stream gives every picture the
same enhancement picture and the same metadata as before, but four pictures
after the resynchronization at its end by picture order, which now have the
RPU of their own access unit; after seeks and in files that start later,
every picture without its enhancement picture whose access unit the module
was given with its time has its own RPU.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c                 | 247 +++++++++++++++++-
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.h                 |  23 ++
 .../DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp   |  43 ++-
 3 files changed, 297 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
index 92fd517..c2ca5c5 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.c
@@ -77,6 +77,13 @@ struct dvbridge_fel_rpu {
  * decoded (dvbridge_fel_base_metadata()): more than the base decoder holds back, and than the
  * pictures between an access unit and the base picture it is presented with */
 #define RING_MAX 32
+/* Hades: the RPUs of the enhancement access units whose time is known, kept for their base pictures should those
+ * go out without their enhancement picture (dvbridge_fel_take() 4, dvbridge_fel_layer_rpu()) */
+#define OWN_MAX MAP_MAX
+/* Base packets that a base picture without its enhancement picture waits for, after its own, for the access unit
+ * that brings its RPU: when the layers are coded in different picture order, that access unit can come in a later
+ * packet than the base picture of its time (one later in the FEL test stream). */
+#define OWN_WAIT_PACKETS 2
 
 /* As dovi_split frames what it gives: a length of this many bytes before every unit when the
  * enhancement layer has an hvcC configuration, start codes (0) otherwise. */
@@ -204,6 +211,21 @@ struct dvbridge_fel {
     bool marked; /* a mark was made since the layer last started */
     unsigned not_needed, wanted;  /* base pictures that went out with a mark, by its kind */
     unsigned decoded, not_decoded; /* enhancement access units given to the decoder, and not */
+    /* Hades: every base picture goes out with the RPU of its own enhancement access unit, also without its
+     * enhancement picture. own: the RPU of each access unit whose time is known (it was given to the decoder, or
+     * passed over in a stream paired by its times), with the time of the base
+     * packet that brought it (carrier), whose base picture the base decoder gives with the same RPU parsed (the
+     * ring). packet_carrier: that time, for each queued access unit. recent: the last base packets, by when they
+     * came (submitted counts them), to know how long a picture may wait for its access unit; last_base: the time
+     * of the last base picture the base decoder gave (dvbridge_fel_base_picture()), to know whether a carrier is
+     * still to come. */
+    int64_t packet_carrier[QUEUE_MAX];
+    struct { int64_t pts, carrier; struct dvbridge_fel_rpu rpu; } own[OWN_MAX];
+    unsigned num_own;
+    struct { int64_t pts; uint64_t seq; } recent[BASE_TIMES_MAX];
+    uint64_t submitted;
+    int64_t last_base;
+    unsigned own_given; /* base pictures that went out without their enhancement picture, with its RPU */
 };
 
 /* Hades: whether two times are the same but for what a time may lose on its way here. */
@@ -348,6 +370,120 @@ static void forget_ring(struct dvbridge_fel *f)
     f->next_ring = 0;
 }
 
+/* Hades: what the base decoder made of an RPU, among the last base pictures it gave; NULL when none of them came
+ * with it */
+static const AVBufferRef *ring_find(const struct dvbridge_fel *f, const struct dvbridge_fel_rpu *rpu)
+{
+    for (unsigned k = 0; rpu->size && k < RING_MAX; ++k)
+        if (f->ring[k].parsed && f->ring[k].coded.size == rpu->size &&
+            !memcmp(f->ring[k].coded.data, rpu->data, rpu->size))
+            return f->ring[k].parsed;
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+/* Hades: a frame without a picture that carries an RPU as coded and as parsed, as the enhancement decoder would
+ * have attached them to its picture; NULL when it cannot be made */
+static AVFrame *metadata_frame(int64_t pts, const struct dvbridge_fel_rpu *rpu, const AVBufferRef *parsed)
+{
+    AVFrame *frame = av_frame_alloc();
+    if (!frame)
+        return NULL;
+    frame->pts = pts;
+    AVBufferRef *metadata = av_buffer_ref(parsed);
+    AVFrameSideData *coded = av_frame_new_side_data(frame, AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_RPU_BUFFER, rpu->size);
+    if (!metadata || !coded ||
+        !av_frame_new_side_data_from_buf(frame, AV_FRAME_DATA_DOVI_METADATA, metadata)) {
+        av_buffer_unref(&metadata);
+        av_frame_free(&frame);
+        return NULL;
+    }
+    memcpy(coded->data, rpu->data, rpu->size);
+    return frame;
+}
+
+static void own_remove(struct dvbridge_fel *f, unsigned i)
+{
+    av_freep(&f->own[i].rpu.data);
+    --f->num_own;
+    memmove(f->own + i, f->own + i + 1, (f->num_own - i) * sizeof(*f->own));
+}
+
+static void own_forget(struct dvbridge_fel *f)
+{
+    while (f->num_own)
+        own_remove(f, f->num_own - 1);
+}
+
+/* Hades: the RPU of the enhancement access unit of the base picture of time pts (taken from *rpu, which is left
+ * empty; an access unit without an RPU of its own leaves an empty one, which says so). carrier: the time of the
+ * base packet that brought it. */
+static void own_add(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, int64_t carrier, struct dvbridge_fel_rpu *rpu)
+{
+    if (pts == AV_NOPTS_VALUE) {
+        av_freep(&rpu->data);
+        *rpu = (struct dvbridge_fel_rpu){0};
+        return;
+    }
+    unsigned i = 0;
+    while (i < f->num_own && f->own[i].pts != pts)
+        ++i;
+    if (i < f->num_own)
+        own_remove(f, i);
+    else if (f->num_own == OWN_MAX)
+        own_remove(f, 0);
+    f->own[f->num_own].pts = pts;
+    f->own[f->num_own].carrier = carrier;
+    f->own[f->num_own++].rpu = *rpu;
+    *rpu = (struct dvbridge_fel_rpu){0};
+}
+
+static int own_find(const struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, int64_t slack)
+{
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < f->num_own; ++i)
+        if (same_time(f->own[i].pts, pts, slack))
+            return (int)i;
+    return -1;
+}
+
+/* Base pictures are asked for in the order they are presented: what is kept for an earlier time is of a picture
+ * that was asked for, or that is not asked for. */
+static void own_drop_before(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, int64_t slack)
+{
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < f->num_own;) {
+        if (f->own[i].pts < pts && !same_time(f->own[i].pts, pts, slack))
+            own_remove(f, i);
+        else
+            ++i;
+    }
+}
+
+/* Hades: the base packets that came after the one of time pts; UINT64_MAX when it is not among the last ones */
+static uint64_t packets_after(const struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, int64_t slack)
+{
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < BASE_TIMES_MAX; ++i)
+        if (f->recent[i].pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE && same_time(f->recent[i].pts, pts, slack))
+            return f->submitted - f->recent[i].seq;
+    return UINT64_MAX;
+}
+
+/* Hades: the RPU of a split access unit of the layer, as FFmpeg's HEVC decoder takes it (dvbridge_mel.h), into
+ * *rpu: none (size 0) when it has none of its own. False when it could not be copied. */
+static bool layer_rpu(const struct dvbridge_fel *f, const AVPacket *packet, struct dvbridge_fel_rpu *rpu)
+{
+    struct dvbridge_rpu_find find = {0};
+    dvbridge_rpu_units(packet->data, (size_t)packet->size, f->layer_length_size,
+                       dvbridge_rpu_find_unit, &find);
+    *rpu = (struct dvbridge_fel_rpu){0};
+    if (!find.rpu)
+        return true;
+    const size_t size = rpu_length(find.rpu + 2, find.size - 2);
+    rpu->data = av_memdup(find.rpu + 2, size);
+    if (size && !rpu->data)
+        return false;
+    rpu->size = size;
+    return true;
+}
+
 static void clear_queues(struct dvbridge_fel *f)
 {
     for (unsigned i = 0; i < f->num_packets; ++i) {
@@ -402,6 +538,7 @@ void dvbridge_fel_destroy(struct dvbridge_fel *f)
         return;
     clear_queues(f);
     forget_ring(f);
+    own_forget(f);
     av_parser_close(f->base_order.parser);
     av_parser_close(f->enhancement_order.parser);
     avcodec_free_context(&f->base_order.context);
@@ -429,6 +566,9 @@ struct dvbridge_fel *dvbridge_fel_create(const AVCodecParameters *p, AVRational
     if (f->apart_max < 0) /* a time base in which it does not fit */
         f->apart_max = INT64_MAX;
     forget_base_times(f, true);
+    f->last_base = AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < BASE_TIMES_MAX; ++i)
+        f->recent[i].pts = AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
     /* Hades: the RPU stays with the enhancement access unit (el_rpu), and the decoder attaches
      * it to the enhancement picture: it is the metadata of that picture, which is not the base
      * picture of the same packet when the layers are coded in different picture order. */
@@ -603,7 +743,9 @@ static bool pump(struct dvbridge_fel *f)
                 goto fail;
             f->fed = true;
             ++f->decoded;
-            av_freep(&f->packet_rpu[0].data);
+            /* Hades: its RPU stays for its base picture, should that go out without its enhancement picture
+             * (a picture that refers to one that was not decoded does not come, nor one that is late) */
+            own_add(f, pts, f->packet_carrier[0], &f->packet_rpu[0]);
         }
         if (!timed) {
             --f->num_times;
@@ -618,6 +760,7 @@ static bool pump(struct dvbridge_fel *f)
         memmove(f->packet_time, f->packet_time + 1, f->num_packets * sizeof(*f->packet_time));
         memmove(f->packet_need, f->packet_need + 1, f->num_packets * sizeof(*f->packet_need));
         memmove(f->packet_rpu, f->packet_rpu + 1, f->num_packets * sizeof(*f->packet_rpu));
+        memmove(f->packet_carrier, f->packet_carrier + 1, f->num_packets * sizeof(*f->packet_carrier));
         if (!receive_frames(f))
             goto fail;
     }
@@ -696,6 +839,10 @@ bool dvbridge_fel_submit(struct dvbridge_fel *f, const AVPacket *packet)
      * the enhancement access unit of this packet, with the mappings that earlier RPUs sent */
     const enum dvbridge_rpu_residual rpu =
         dvbridge_rpu_nlq_packet(&f->rpu, packet->data, (size_t)packet->size, f->base_length_size);
+    /* Hades: and when it came, for a base picture that waits for the access unit that brings its RPU */
+    ++f->submitted;
+    f->recent[f->submitted % BASE_TIMES_MAX].pts = packet->pts;
+    f->recent[f->submitted % BASE_TIMES_MAX].seq = f->submitted;
     if (f->failed || f->draining)
         return false;
     /* By picture order every base packet needs its time, which an enhancement picture takes.
@@ -783,16 +930,21 @@ bool dvbridge_fel_submit(struct dvbridge_fel *f, const AVPacket *packet)
             goto fail;
         }
         if (!picture_identity(&f->enhancement_order, copy, &f->packet_order[f->num_packets])) {
-            av_packet_free(&copy);
             /* Hades: while the layer waits for a picture to start at, an access unit that cannot
              * be read is one that cannot start it, like any other. After a seek the parser may
              * have the parameter sets of the layer only from its next random-access picture on:
              * a stream of two tracks brings them with those pictures and nowhere else. */
             if (f->synchronizing) {
+                /* Hades: by its time, its RPU stays for its base picture */
+                struct dvbridge_fel_rpu own;
+                if (f->timed && time != AV_NOPTS_VALUE && layer_rpu(f, copy, &own))
+                    own_add(f, time, packet->pts, &own);
+                av_packet_free(&copy);
                 f->num_times = 0;
                 ++f->preroll_packets;
                 continue;
             }
+            av_packet_free(&copy);
             f->reason = "the picture order of an enhancement picture could not be parsed";
             goto fail;
         }
@@ -824,6 +976,10 @@ bool dvbridge_fel_submit(struct dvbridge_fel *f, const AVPacket *packet)
              * layer presents before that picture cannot be decoded from it, or is not known to
              * be: those base pictures go out without the layer. */
             if (f->enhancement_order.parser->key_frame != 1) {
+                /* Hades: its RPU stays for the base picture of its time */
+                struct dvbridge_fel_rpu own;
+                if (layer_rpu(f, copy, &own))
+                    own_add(f, time, packet->pts, &own);
                 av_packet_free(&copy);
                 ++f->preroll_packets;
                 continue;
@@ -878,6 +1034,7 @@ bool dvbridge_fel_submit(struct dvbridge_fel *f, const AVPacket *packet)
             f->packet_rpu[f->num_packets].size = size;
         }
         f->packet_time[f->num_packets] = time;
+        f->packet_carrier[f->num_packets] = packet->pts;
         f->packet_bytes += copy->size;
         f->packets[f->num_packets++] = copy;
     }
@@ -971,6 +1128,60 @@ void dvbridge_fel_base_metadata(struct dvbridge_fel *f, const uint8_t *coded, si
     f->ring[k].parsed = metadata;
 }
 
+void dvbridge_fel_base_picture(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts)
+{
+    if (f && pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE && (f->last_base == AV_NOPTS_VALUE || pts > f->last_base))
+        f->last_base = pts;
+}
+
+/* Hades: the answer for a base picture of time pts that goes out without its enhancement picture: 4, with a frame
+ * that carries the RPU of its own enhancement access unit and the metadata that the base decoder made of it, when
+ * the module knows them; 0 while one of them is still to come; 2 otherwise (the picture keeps the RPU carried with
+ * it, as before). may_come: its access unit may come in a packet that is still to come (it is not known to have been
+ * passed over): it is waited for, for a few base packets after the one of its time. */
+static int without_layer(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, int64_t slack, bool may_come, AVFrame **frame)
+{
+    const int i = own_find(f, pts, slack);
+    if (i < 0)
+        return may_come && packets_after(f, pts, slack) < OWN_WAIT_PACKETS ? 0 : 2;
+    const struct dvbridge_fel_rpu *rpu = &f->own[i].rpu;
+    const AVBufferRef *parsed = rpu->size ? ring_find(f, rpu) : NULL;
+    if (rpu->size && !parsed && f->own[i].carrier != AV_NOPTS_VALUE &&
+        f->last_base != AV_NOPTS_VALUE && f->own[i].carrier > f->last_base)
+        return 0; /* the base picture that brought it is still to come */
+    AVFrame *made = parsed ? metadata_frame(pts, rpu, parsed) : NULL;
+    own_remove(f, (unsigned)i);
+    if (!made)
+        return 2; /* no RPU of its own (it keeps the one before), or none that can be had */
+    ++f->own_given;
+    *frame = made;
+    return 4;
+}
+
+int dvbridge_fel_layer_rpu(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, AVFrame **frame)
+{
+    if (!f || !frame || *frame || pts == AV_NOPTS_VALUE)
+        return 0;
+    const int64_t slack = f->timed ? f->tolerance : 0;
+    if (f->timed && f->zero_twice && same_time(pts, f->zero, f->tolerance))
+        return 0;
+    own_drop_before(f, pts, slack);
+    const int i = own_find(f, pts, slack);
+    const AVBufferRef *parsed = i >= 0 ? ring_find(f, &f->own[i].rpu) : NULL;
+    AVFrame *made = parsed ? metadata_frame(pts, &f->own[i].rpu, parsed) : NULL;
+    if (!made)
+        return 0;
+    own_remove(f, (unsigned)i);
+    ++f->own_given;
+    *frame = made;
+    return 1;
+}
+
+unsigned dvbridge_fel_own_rpus(const struct dvbridge_fel *f)
+{
+    return f ? f->own_given : 0;
+}
+
 int dvbridge_fel_take(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, AVFrame **frame)
 {
     if (!f || !frame || *frame || pts == AV_NOPTS_VALUE || !pump(f))
@@ -1001,8 +1212,16 @@ int dvbridge_fel_take(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, AVFrame **frame)
         --f->num_skipped;
         memmove(f->skipped + i, f->skipped + i + 1, (f->num_skipped - i) * sizeof(*f->skipped));
     }
-    if (f->synchronizing || (f->anchor_pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE && pts < f->anchor_pts))
-        return 2; /* Preroll before a recoverable EL picture, not a substitute. */
+    /* Hades: (likewise what is kept of the RPUs of the access units of earlier times) */
+    own_drop_before(f, pts, slack);
+    /* Preroll before a recoverable EL picture, not a substitute.
+     * Hades: with the RPU of its own access unit when the module knows it (not for a time that is
+     * not of one picture alone). */
+    if (f->synchronizing || (f->anchor_pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE && pts < f->anchor_pts)) {
+        /* (by picture order, while the layer waits, the time of an access unit is not known) */
+        const bool may_come = f->timed || !f->synchronizing;
+        return ambiguous ? 2 : without_layer(f, pts, slack, may_come, frame);
+    }
     for (unsigned i = 0; i < f->num_frames;) {
         AVFrame *candidate = f->frames[i];
         if (candidate->pts > pts && candidate->pts - pts > slack) {
@@ -1015,6 +1234,10 @@ int dvbridge_fel_take(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, AVFrame **frame)
         if (!ambiguous && (candidate->pts >= pts || pts - candidate->pts <= slack)) {
             candidate->pts = pts;
             *frame = candidate;
+            /* Hades: (its RPU comes with its enhancement picture) */
+            const int own = own_find(f, pts, slack);
+            if (own >= 0)
+                own_remove(f, (unsigned)own);
             return 1;
         }
         av_frame_free(&candidate);
@@ -1033,8 +1256,12 @@ int dvbridge_fel_take(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t pts, AVFrame **frame)
     /* Hades: so does a mark of a later time, left by an access unit that came after this one's
      * in the order they are given (the decoder had given all it held before any mark was made) */
     if (f->timed && (f->num_frames || f->num_skipped)) {
-        ++f->passed_missing;
-        return 2;
+        /* Hades: (its access unit came before the one of that later picture, if it came: with the RPU of its
+         * own access unit when the module knows it) */
+        const int answer = without_layer(f, pts, slack, false, frame);
+        if (answer)
+            ++f->passed_missing;
+        return answer;
     }
     return f->eof || f->num_frames == QUEUE_MAX ? -1 : 0;
 }
@@ -1075,6 +1302,9 @@ void dvbridge_fel_time_zero(struct dvbridge_fel *f, int64_t zero)
         return;
     f->zero = zero;
     forget_base_times(f, true);
+    /* Hades: the times of what is kept for the RPUs of the base pictures are on the scale before */
+    own_forget(f);
+    f->last_base = AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
 }
 
 void dvbridge_fel_base_flushed(struct dvbridge_fel *f)
@@ -1086,6 +1316,11 @@ void dvbridge_fel_base_flushed(struct dvbridge_fel *f)
      * the metadata of its pictures is no picture's any more */
     dvbridge_rpu_nlq_forget(&f->rpu);
     forget_ring(f);
+    /* Hades: nor are the RPUs kept for the base pictures that were to come */
+    own_forget(f);
+    f->last_base = AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < BASE_TIMES_MAX; ++i)
+        f->recent[i].pts = AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
 }
 
 void dvbridge_fel_layer_skip_counts(const struct dvbridge_fel *f,
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.h b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.h
index 61cca14..53017ec 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.h
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_fel.h
@@ -25,6 +25,15 @@ bool dvbridge_fel_drain(struct dvbridge_fel *fel);
  * was not decoded: its RPU can carry a residual and the layer, not decoded, waited for its next
  * random-access picture to start at again, or it is a leading picture of the one it started at,
  * whose picture does not come. It goes out without the layer, as with 2, with that metadata.
+ * Also, where the answer would be 2, for a base picture whose enhancement access unit the module
+ * knows (the stream gave its time, or it was given to the decoder): with the RPU of that access
+ * unit, as coded, and the metadata that the base
+ * decoder made of it (dvbridge_fel_base_metadata()). So a base picture that goes out without its
+ * enhancement picture has the metadata it has with it, also where the layers are coded in
+ * different picture order and the RPU carried with the base picture is the one of another
+ * picture. 0 is also the answer while that access unit, or the base picture that brought its
+ * RPU, may still come (dvbridge_fel_base_picture()); 2, with the RPU carried with the base
+ * picture, where the module does not know it.
  * Hades: exact to the unit of the time base; in a stream that gives the times of its
  * enhancement pictures (DVBRIDGE_FEL_LAYER_TIME), to the half millisecond that a time may lose
  * on its way here. In such a stream 2 is also the answer for a base picture whose enhancement
@@ -111,4 +120,18 @@ void dvbridge_fel_layer_skip_counts(const struct dvbridge_fel *fel,
  * (dvbridge_fel_take()). */
 void dvbridge_fel_base_metadata(struct dvbridge_fel *fel, const uint8_t *coded, size_t coded_size,
                                 const uint8_t *parsed, size_t parsed_size);
+/* Hades: a base picture came out of the base decoder, at this time (each one, before
